  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_18433",
  "verbalization": "Decitabine is implicated in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(6;9)(p23;q34) through a mechanism that involves its interaction with leukemia cells. The evidence suggests that Decitabine is linked to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, a closely related subtype, and that this condition is further associated with Idarubicin, which in turn is linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(6;9)(p23;q34). This indicates a potential pathway where Decitabine may exert its therapeutic effect by targeting the underlying cellular processes of leukemia, possibly through DNA methylation or other epigenetic mechanisms. The shared indication with Idarubicin suggests a possible overlapping mechanism of action, though the exact relationship between Decitabine and Idarubicin remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for Decitabine in the treatment of this leukemia subtype, but further research is needed to clarify its specific mechanism and clinical relevance.",
